{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5ce2sbogakjhr7kxfq6nusbavwggdg27hega5d4vlaf37tyejo6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01D9iuoicjuaWpN2n3N3UhBU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iRpL4E/translated_rust/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — Phase B configuration surface\n\n## Build-time configurations (enumerated mechanically)\n\n### Cargo features\n\n`Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` section** and no optional dependencies:\n\n```\n$ grep -n -A20 '\\[features\\]' Cargo.toml   # -> no match\n```\n\nTherefore the feature power-set has exactly **one** element:\n\n| # | feature combination | command |\n|---|---------------------|---------|\n| F1 | *(empty — default == `--no-default-features`)* | `cargo check/test --no-default-features` |\n\n`--all-features` is identical to F1. Both are exercised by\n`scripts/check_all_features.sh` (which enumerates the power-set of\n`[features]` from `Cargo.toml` and falls back to the empty set), so the\n\"every feature combination\" requirement collapses to this single configuration.\n\n### C build-time configurations\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` declares one target and no options:\n`add_executable(driver src/main.c)` + `target_compile_options(driver PRIVATE\n-fno-strict-aliasing)`. `c_src/src/main.c` contains **no `#ifdef`/`#if`** at all\n(only `#include <stdio.h>` and `<string.h>`), so there is exactly one C\nconfiguration. The differential `.so` is built from the same single translation\nunit with the same flag.\n\n### Crate targets (both are verified)\n\n| # | target | product | note |\n|---|--------|---------|------|\n| T1 | `[lib] crate-type=[\"cdylib\"]` | `target/<profile>/libdriver.so` | loaded with `libloading` in all differential tests |\n| T2 | `[[bin]] driver` (`#![no_main]`) | `target/<profile>/driver` | compared against the CMake executable `c_src/build/driver` |\n| T3 | `--release` profile (`panic = \"abort\"`) | both of the above | re-run of the whole suite in release mode |\n\n## Runtime configuration axes (derived from the C branches)\n\nThe C code branches on exactly these things:\n\n* **A1 — entry point**: `driver` (lowest-level exported function) vs `main`\n  (reads stdin, then calls `driver`).\n* **A2 — `driver`'s `int floors` value**: the only datum that varies in the\n  output; every byte of the 4-byte little-endian image can vary\n  (`print_hex` loops over the raw struct image).\n* **A3 — stdin byte shape for `scanf(\"%d\")`**: leading-whitespace class (each of\n  the six `isspace` bytes and mixtures, incl. crossing newlines), sign\n  (`none`/`+`/`-`), digit-run length, leading zeros, terminator class\n  (EOF / whitespace / letter / punctuation), trailing junk, extra numbers.\n* **A4 — magnitude class**: fits in `int` / fits in `long` but not `int`\n  (truncation) / exceeds `long` (glibc saturation). This is the only place the\n  C's numeric behaviour is non-obvious.\n* **A5 — stdin delivery**: pipe vs regular file vs `/dev/null` vs closed fd\n  (glibc picks a different buffering path for each; the Rust `std` reader must\n  agree byte-for-byte).\n* **A6 — stdout delivery**: pipe (line/full-buffered decision) vs regular file.\n* **A7 — calls per process**: `driver` once vs many times in one process\n  (stream/flush state must not alter the byte stream).\n\nCross-product pruned to the combinations the code actually distinguishes:\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n| C1 | `driver` via `.so` | `floors = 0` (all-zero image) | [x] |\n| C2 | `driver` via `.so` | `floors = 1`, `-1`, `2`, `-2` (small ± values) | [x] |\n| C3 | `driver` via `.so` | `floors = INT_MAX (2147483647)` and `INT_MIN (-2147483648)` (A2 extremes) | [x] |\n| C4 | `driver` via `.so` | `floors` = every single-byte pattern `0x000000ff`, `0x0000ff00`, `0x00ff0000`, `0xff000000`, `0x7f7f7f7f`, `0x80808080`, `0xdeadbeef`, `0xffffffff` (exercises every hex nibble position of `print_hex`) | [x] |\n| C5 | `driver` via `.so` | `floors` = all 32 powers of two and their negations | [x] |\n| C6 | `driver` via `.so` | 4096 uniformly random `i32` (fixed seed, property-style) | [x] |\n| C7 | `driver` via `.so` | A7: 4096 calls in **one** process (`driver-batch`) — repeated-call/flush state | [x] |\n| C8 | `driver` via `.so` | A6: stdout is a **regular file** instead of a pipe (buffering-mode difference) | [x] |\n| C9 | `main` via `.so` | plain decimal, no sign, no whitespace, EOF terminator: `0`, `1`, `7`, `42` | [x] |\n| C10 | `main` via `.so` | A3 sign axis: `+N` and `-N` for N in {0,1,7,42,2147483647,2147483648} | [x] |\n| C11 | `main` via `.so` | A3 whitespace axis: each of ` `, `\\t`, `\\n`, `\\v`, `\\f`, `\\r` (single, repeated, and mixed, crossing newlines) before the number | [x] |\n| C12 | `main` via `.so` | A3 terminator axis: number followed by EOF / `\\n` / ` ` / `\\t` / `x` / `.` / `,` / `-` / a second number | [x] |\n| C13 | `main` via `.so` | A3 leading-zero axis: `0`, `00`, `007`, 1 / 18 / 19 / 20 / 5000 leading zeros before a value | [x] |\n| C14 | `main` via `.so` | A3 digit-run length 1…25 digits of `9`s and of `1234567890…` (crosses `int`, `long`, saturation) | [x] |\n| C15 | `main` via `.so` | A4 in-`int` boundaries: `2147483646`, `2147483647`, `-2147483647`, `-2147483648`, `65535`, `65536` | [x] |\n| C16 | `main` via `.so` | A4 in-`long`-not-`int` (truncating): `2147483648`, `-2147483649`, `4294967295`, `4294967296`, `4294967297`, `-4294967296`, `1099511627776`, `1234567890123` | [x] |\n| C17 | `main` via `.so` | A4 `long` boundary / saturation: `9223372036854775806/7/8`, `-9223372036854775807/8/9`, `18446744073709551616`, 40-digit and 1000-digit numbers (± ) | [x] |\n| C18 | `main` via `.so` | 2048 randomized stdin strings (fixed seed) mixing all of A3/A4: random whitespace prefix, random sign, random digit count 1…24, random trailing junk | [x] |\n| C19 | `main` via `.so` | A5: stdin from a **regular file** (glibc block-buffered path) with the same random corpus | [x] |\n| C20 | `main` via `.so` | A5: stdin = `/dev/null` (immediate EOF, character device) | [x] |\n| C21 | `main` via `.so` | A5: stdin is a pipe closed after a **partial** number, i.e. no terminator byte (`42`, `-`, `+`, `0`) | [x] |\n| C22 | `main` via `.so` | multi-line input where the first line is whitespace only (`scanf` crosses newlines — `fgets` would not) | [x] |\n| C23 | executable (T2) | whole binary vs CMake `c_src/build/driver`: the full C9–C22 stdin corpus through the real process entry point | [x] |\n| C24 | both `.so` exports | T3: entire suite re-run with `--release` (`panic = \"abort\"`, optimizations) | [x] |\n| C25 | both `.so` exports | symbol-resolution config: `dlopen` + `dlsym(\"driver\")`, `dlsym(\"main\")` on both libraries, and `nm -D` export-set equality | [x] |\n\nAll rows are checked off by the tests in `tests/differential.rs` (subprocess\nisolation via `examples/so_runner.rs`, one fresh process per `main` case) and\n`tests/inprocess.rs` (in-process `libloading` + `dup2` stdout capture, both\nlibraries in the same process). Randomized rows use a fixed-seed xorshift PRNG\nso failures are reproducible.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3139,"cache_read_input_tokens":68077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3139,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b2607ca-6e3e-49ad-87bc-6f2052e63da2","uuid":"6dd78188-40b6-486f-b9b7-5484ca44010d","timestamp":"2026-08-18T11:46:58.457Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01D9iuoicjuaWpN2n3N3UhBU","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iRpL4E/translated_rust/CONFIGS.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b2607ca-6e3e-49ad-87bc-6f2052e63da2","uuid":"0a0086e4-c4ca-481d-94d3-4425c3711395","timestamp":"2026-08-18T11:46:58.467Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-iRpL4E/translated_rust/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — Phase B configuration surface\n\n## Build-time configurations (enumerated mechanically)\n\n### Cargo features\n\n`Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` section** and no optional dependencies:\n\n```\n$ grep -n -A20 '\\[features\\]' Cargo.toml   # -> no match\n```\n\nTherefore the feature power-set has exactly **one** element:\n\n| # | feature combination | command |\n|---|---------------------|---------|\n| F1 | *(empty — default == `--no-default-features`)* | `cargo check/test --no-default-features` |\n\n`--all-features` is identical to F1. Both are exercised by\n`scripts/check_all_features.sh` (which enumerates the power-set of\n`[features]` from `Cargo.toml` and falls back to the empty set), so the\n\"every feature combination\" requirement collapses to this single configuration.\n\n### C build-time configurations\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` declares one target and no options:\n`add_executable(driver src/main.c)` + `target_compile_options(driver PRIVATE\n-fno-strict-aliasing)`. `c_src/src/main.c` contains **no `#ifdef`/`#if`** at all\n(only `#include <stdio.h>` and `<string.h>`), so there is exactly one C\nconfiguration. The differential `.so` is built from the same single translation\nunit with the same flag.\n\n### Crate targets (both are verified)\n\n| # | target | product | note |\n|---|--------|---------|------|\n| T1 | `[lib] crate-type=[\"cdylib\"]` | `target/<profile>/libdriver.so` | loaded with `libloading` in all differential tests |\n| T2 | `[[bin]] driver` (`#![no_main]`) | `target/<profile>/driver` | compared against the CMake executable `c_src/build/driver` |\n| T3 | `--release` profile (`panic = \"abort\"`) | both of the above | re-run of the whole suite in release mode |\n\n## Runtime configuration axes (derived from the C branches)\n\nThe C code branches on exactly these things:\n\n* **A1 — entry point**: `driver` (lowest-level exported function) vs `main`\n  (reads stdin, then calls `driver`).\n* **A2 — `driver`'s `int floors` value**: the only datum that varies in the\n  output; every byte of the 4-byte little-endian image can vary\n  (`print_hex` loops over the raw struct image).\n* **A3 — stdin byte shape for `scanf(\"%d\")`**: leading-whitespace class (each of\n  the six `isspace` bytes and mixtures, incl. crossing newlines), sign\n  (`none`/`+`/`-`), digit-run length, leading zeros, terminator class\n  (EOF / whitespace / letter / punctuation), trailing junk, extra numbers.\n* **A4 — magnitude class**: fits in `int` / fits in `long` but not `int`\n  (truncation) / exceeds `long` (glibc saturation). This is the only place the\n  C's numeric behaviour is non-obvious.\n* **A5 — stdin delivery**: pipe vs regular file vs `/dev/null` vs closed fd\n  (glibc picks a different buffering path for each; the Rust `std` reader must\n  agree byte-for-byte).\n* **A6 — stdout delivery**: pipe (line/full-buffered decision) vs regular file.\n* **A7 — calls per process**: `driver` once vs many times in one process\n  (stream/flush state must not alter the byte stream).\n\nCross-product pruned to the combinations the code actually distinguishes:\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n| C1 | `driver` via `.so` | `floors = 0` (all-zero image) | [x] |\n| C2 | `driver` via `.so` | `floors = 1`, `-1`, `2`, `-2` (small ± values) | [x] |\n| C3 | `driver` via `.so` | `floors = INT_MAX (2147483647)` and `INT_MIN (-2147483648)` (A2 extremes) | [x] |\n| C4 | `driver` via `.so` | `floors` = every single-byte pattern `0x000000ff`, `0x0000ff00`, `0x00ff0000`, `0xff000000`, `0x7f7f7f7f`, `0x80808080`, `0xdeadbeef`, `0xffffffff` (exercises every hex nibble position of `print_hex`) | [x] |\n| C5 | `driver` via `.so` | `floors` = all 32 powers of two and their negations | [x] |\n| C6 | `driver` via `.so` | 4096 uniformly random `i32` (fixed seed, property-style) | [x] |\n| C7 | `driver` via `.so` | A7: 4096 calls in **one** process (`driver-batch`) — repeated-call/flush state | [x] |\n| C8 | `driver` via `.so` | A6: stdout is a **regular file** instead of a pipe (buffering-mode difference) | [x] |\n| C9 | `main` via `.so` | plain decimal, no sign, no whitespace, EOF terminator: `0`, `1`, `7`, `42` | [x] |\n| C10 | `main` via `.so` | A3 sign axis: `+N` and `-N` for N in {0,1,7,42,2147483647,2147483648} | [x] |\n| C11 | `main` via `.so` | A3 whitespace axis: each of ` `, `\\t`, `\\n`, `\\v`, `\\f`, `\\r` (single, repeated, and mixed, crossing newlines) before the number | [x] |\n| C12 | `main` via `.so` | A3 terminator axis: number followed by EOF / `\\n` / ` ` / `\\t` / `x` / `.` / `,` / `-` / a second number | [x] |\n| C13 | `main` via `.so` | A3 leading-zero axis: `0`, `00`, `007`, 1 / 18 / 19 / 20 / 5000 leading zeros before a value | [x] |\n| C14 | `main` via `.so` | A3 digit-run length 1…25 digits of `9`s and of `1234567890…` (crosses `int`, `long`, saturation) | [x] |\n| C15 | `main` via `.so` | A4 in-`int` boundaries: `2147483646`, `2147483647`, `-2147483647`, `-2147483648`, `65535`, `65536` | [x] |\n| C16 | `main` via `.so` | A4 in-`long`-not-`int` (truncating): `2147483648`, `-2147483649`, `4294967295`, `4294967296`, `4294967297`, `-4294967296`, `1099511627776`, `1234567890123` | [x] |\n| C17 | `main` via `.so` | A4 `long` boundary / saturation: `9223372036854775806/7/8`, `-9223372036854775807/8/9`, `18446744073709551616`, 40-digit and 1000-digit numbers (± ) | [x] |\n| C18 | `main` via `.so` | 2048 randomized stdin strings (fixed seed) mixing all of A3/A4: random whitespace prefix, random sign, random digit count 1…24, random trailing junk | [x] |\n| C19 | `main` via `.so` | A5: stdin from a **regular file** (glibc block-buffered path) with the same random corpus | [x] |\n| C20 | `main` via `.so` | A5: stdin = `/dev/null` (immediate EOF, character device) | [x] |\n| C21 | `main` via `.so` | A5: stdin is a pipe closed after a **partial** number, i.e. no terminator byte (`42`, `-`, `+`, `0`) | [x] |\n| C22 | `main` via `.so` | multi-line input where the first line is whitespace only (`scanf` crosses newlines — `fgets` would not) | [x] |\n| C23 | executable (T2) | whole binary vs CMake `c_src/build/driver`: the full C9–C22 stdin corpus through the real process entry point | [x] |\n| C24 | both `.so` exports | T3: entire suite re-run with `--release` (`panic = \"abort\"`, optimizations) | [x] |\n| C25 | both `.so` exports | symbol-resolution config: `dlopen` + `dlsym(\"driver\")`, `dlsym(\"main\")` on both libraries, and `nm -D` export-set equality | [x] |\n\nAll rows are checked off by the tests in `tests/differential.rs` (subprocess\nisolation via `examples/so_runner.rs`, one fresh process per `main` case) and\n`tests/inprocess.rs` (in-process `libloading` + `dup2` stdout capture, both\nlibraries in the same process). Randomized rows use a fixed-seed xorshift PRNG\nso failures are reproducible.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
