{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jyzri6vfvpqv7yjfh6tvfdwrmf7aprpbt6m4jwauoxlsigo4hpqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. Summary:\n\n## What I verified\n\n`c_src/` is a single 55-line translation unit exporting exactly two symbols (`driver`, `main`). I built it both ways (CMake executable + `gcc -shared`) and compared it against the Rust translation through `libloading` — never by calling Rust directly.\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (all mechanically derived from the C source):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — every `nm -D` symbol; C exports `driver main`, Rust exports `driver main`, **diff empty**; `ldd` shows 0 unresolved deps.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 25 rows (E1–E25). The C has no error macros/asserts/range checks at all: the entire rejection surface is `scanf(\"%d\")`, whose result the C *ignores*, plus write-side failures.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 33 rows (C1–C32 + C26b) over 8 axes the C actually branches on, plus the build matrix (`[features]` is empty → 1 combination, verified in dev **and** release).\n\n**Result: 54 differential tests pass** (subprocess-isolated `libloading` host) plus a `harness = false` in-process test comparing **20 217** `driver` calls with `dup2` stdout capture — in dev, release, `--no-default-features`, default and `--all-features`.\n\n## Three real divergences found and fixed (C never touched)\n\n1. **No C ABI surface at all** — the crate was bin-only and exported nothing. Added a `cdylib` sharing one impl file with `#[no_mangle] driver`/`main`, so the symbol diff reaches empty.\n2. **`SIGPIPE` mismatch** — measured: C dies with signal 13 on a closed stdout pipe, Rust with a normal `fn main` exits 0 (std installs `SIG_IGN`). Fixed with `#![cfg_attr(not(test), no_main)]`, making the exported `main` the real ELF entry point → signal 13, matching C.\n3. **Blocking on stdin** — the original `read_to_end` hung forever when a pipe stays open after `42\\n`, where C's `scanf` returns immediately. Rewrote the scanf emulation to read byte-at-a-time (digits + one lookahead), with a 3-second deadline test.\n\nI also found and fixed a **harness** bug that would have invalidated everything: `cargo test` rebuilds the cdylib into `deps/` without uplifting it, so the suite was silently comparing a stale `.so`. Path resolution now picks the freshest copy that really exports both symbols and asserts non-staleness (I proved the guard fires).\n\n## Harness self-validation\n\n`scripts/mutation_check.py` injects 21 behaviour-changing bugs (wrong struct fields, big-endian image, uppercase hex, swapped nibbles, `isspace` without `\\v`/`\\n`, `+` mishandling, saturation/truncation swaps, EOF-slurping, read-error handling, wrong return code) and requires the suite to fail for each, plus 2 deliberately equivalent mutants that must survive → `MUTATION CHECK PASSED: 23 mutants behaved as expected`. Every child process has a 60 s watchdog, so hangs fail tests instead of stalling.\n\nReproduce everything with `scripts/verify_all.sh --with-mutation` → `VERIFY_ALL: everything passed`. Findings are written up in `VERIFICATION.md`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":594,"cache_read_input_tokens":279396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":594,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b2607ca-6e3e-49ad-87bc-6f2052e63da2","uuid":"80ee4f2f-993f-407c-a752-999b594f0aa1","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:04:37.420Z"}
